<section class="container py-16"><article class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl">
<h1>Shopify SMS app alternatives</h1>
<p>Start with the job that is failing, then open the guide for the app you currently use. Replacing a sender, a capture form and a managed retention program are different projects. Keep working channels while evaluating the specific replacement; a new email platform need not trigger an SMS move.</p>
<h2>Route your replacement by operating job</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Restore lifecycle journeys:</strong> use the Klaviyo, Omnisend, Drip, Sendlane or ActiveCampaign guide to inventory welcome, recovery, post-purchase and winback. Bring entry events, exclusions and outstanding waits to the trial. Choose on whether your operator can safely edit and stop those journeys.</li>
<li><strong>Replace work performed by people:</strong> start with Rejoiner when strategy, creative production or campaign management is part of the relationship. Decide who inherits the approval queue before comparing software fees. Marsello and Yotpo guides also help scope a move where retention jobs connect to other customer systems; inventory those dependencies first.</li>
<li><strong>Change capture or basic sending:</strong> use Shopify Email, Mailchimp, Brevo, tinyEmail, Privy or Justuno to distinguish forms, audience records and ongoing journeys. If forms work, evaluate whether only downstream automation needs replacement. AfterShip Email and Firepush guides help scope which messaging jobs you actually intend to move.</li>
<li><strong>Change SMS delivery and reply operations:</strong> use Postscript, Attentive, SMSBump or Recart to plan sender, destination, permission and reply ownership. Keep email on its own acceptance checklist. A cheaper message quote does not establish that cart events, withdrawals and support replies work.</li>
</ul>
